 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Why does Russia own land between Poland and Lithuania?",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.74
  },
  {
   "text": "It is Kaliningrad.",
   "start": 3.66,
   "end": 4.5
  },
  {
   "text": "Until 1946, it was K\u00f6nigsberg.",
   "start": 4.98,
   "end": 7.38
  },
  {
   "text": "Teutonic Knights founded it in 1255.",
   "start": 8.08,
   "end": 10.34
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1701, a king was crowned there.",
   "start": 11.08,
   "end": 13.46
  },
  {
   "text": "Kant lived there virtually all his life.",
   "start": 14.2,
   "end": 16.1
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1944, bombs burned the old city.",
   "start": 16.9,
   "end": 19.36
  },
  {
   "text": "In April 1945, the Soviets took it.",
   "start": 20.06,
   "end": 22.54
  },
  {
   "text": "At Potsdam, the Allies agreed to give it to Moscow.",
   "start": 23.18,
   "end": 25.5
  },
  {
   "text": "Renamed Kaliningrad after Mikhail Kalinin, who was unrelated to it.",
   "start": 26.64,
   "end": 30.12
  },
  {
   "text": "Every land link to Russia now crosses NATO and EU.",
   "start": 31.0,
   "end": 33.64
  },
  {
   "text": "A German city became Russian.",
   "start": 34.44,
   "end": 36.06
  },
  {
   "text": "Full story on our channel.",
   "start": 37.0,
   "end": 38.04
  }
 ]
